WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.540
Wally, pay attention. What are you doing over there?

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.480
I'm just explaining a simple fact to Bowers, Mr. Delmar.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.760
What simple fact?

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:11.690
Mary, that in direct view electronic cathode ray tubes, such as you find in our Dumont set,

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:16.640
it's possible to increase dimension without image disintegration or loss of definition.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.070
Well, it may be a fact, but it ain't simple.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:23.670
What do you mean, Professor, is that Dumont television sets are hot stuff?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:24.630
He did?

00:00:25.330 --> 00:00:29.660
Certainly. After all, Dumont pioneered the big direct view tubes right from the start.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:35.450
Dumont makes the kind of big tubes that mean not just bigger pictures, but also brighter, sharper pictures.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.330
You see what I mean? Hot stuff.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:38.090
Yeah, mm-hmm.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.450
Of course, Mr. Delmar.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:46.790
After all, Dumont, uh, Dumont, uh, pioneered these, uh, directing tubes, you know.

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:47.190
Mm-hmm.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:48.620
You see what I mean, Professor?

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.280
Almost not.

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:50.120
Yeah, yeah.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:56.070
Even today, only Dumont makes a giant 20-inch tube, 213 square inches of picture.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:59.890
Now, that's four times as large as the picture you get on most of today's...

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:04.610
television set. Yeah, you understand? You always have to have a little brain to understand.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.110
Yeah. And you do have a little brain, don't you? Oh, certainly, Bowers.

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:12.010
No, no, I... Mr. Delmar, even today,

00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:16.630
I mean, Dumont television receivers all have FM radio

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.870
as well as television, and that's another sign of Dumont quality. Well, that certainly is very

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:24.980
sensational. I would make some remark now, only I think the best thing we should do is to get back

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:29.430
to class. Yes, so go back to your seats, boys. Now, boys and girls,

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:30.520
Uh, we-
